            <ArticleTitle>Size reduction using Mirror Visual Feedback (MVF) reduces phantom pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>357-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/13554790903081767</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following limb amputation patients continue to feel the vivid presence of a phantom limb. A majority of patients also experience pain in the phantom and sometimes (as in our case DS) the pain is severe. Remarkably we find that optically 'resurrecting' the phantom with a mirror and using a lens to make the phantom appear to shrink caused the pain to 'shrink' as well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
